# GrowFlow — Phase 06G: Responsive + Accessibility Foundation

**Status:** FROZEN / AUTHORITATIVE  
**Version:** 1.0  
**Phase:** 06G  
**Depends On:** Phase 06C — Frontend Design Tokens; Phase 06D — Core Component System; Phase 06E — Application Shell; Phase 06F — Frontend Behavior Foundation  
**Aligns With:** Phase 01 — Frontend Page Inventory; Phase 02 — Information Architecture & Navigation; Phase 03 — Visual Design System & Experience Direction; Phase 05 — Application & Integration Architecture  
**Scope:** Responsive behavior, device adaptation, accessibility, keyboard interaction, focus management, assistive technology behavior, motion reduction, content scaling, responsive data interfaces, responsive workflows, testing, and implementation governance.

---

# 01. Purpose

Phase 06G defines how GrowFlow remains usable, accessible, readable, and behaviorally correct across:

- desktop;
- tablet;
- mobile;
- different viewport sizes;
- different input methods;
- keyboard-only navigation;
- screen readers;
- reduced-motion preferences;
- zoom/text scaling;
- slow networks and constrained devices.

This phase is implementation-grade.

It does not redesign the visual system. It defines how the already-frozen GrowFlow system behaves when space, input modality, accessibility preferences, and device capabilities change.

The governing principle is:

> **Responsive design changes presentation and interaction mechanics, never domain meaning or security semantics.**

